# Claim-bearing paths. A change to any of these blocks git commit/push until
# .claim-review-ack accounts for the file with a resolving EVIDENCE pointer or
# a recorded OVERRIDE. One glob per line; matched against full path and basename.
index.html
about/index.html
resume/index.html
suite/*.html
suite/*.py
# suite/sources.json is deliberately NOT listed. It is claim-bearing, and it is gated by
# .githooks/sources_receipt.py, which re-fetches the new pinned url and compares its sha256
# to the manifest. Listing it here as well policed one file under two grammars: the generic
# loop accepts only EVIDENCE/OVERRIDE, so the PIN receipt that checker demands was rejected
# as malformed, and passing required two receipt lines in a specific order. The stronger
# checker owns the file, including its audit record.
stack/*.html
stack/*.js
eval-compare/index.html
*.md
docs/*.json
registry.json
*results*.json
*manifest*.json

# installed via: git config core.hooksPath .githooks
